1
00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:05,140
Three measured re-runs of agent-runtime-evals on main.

2
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:08,490
Three runs each, one model, one prompt.

3
00:00:08,650 --> 00:00:12,420
Pass per run: twenty-one, twenty-one, twenty.

4
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,860
Then twenty-six, twenty-three, twenty-six.

5
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:19,240
Then twenty-five, twenty-five, twenty-six.

6
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:25,340
Original twenty-four cases: sixty-two, sixty-six, sixty-seven of seventy-two.

7
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:30,000
The failure found: a refund claimed without a confirmed write.

8
00:00:30,090 --> 00:00:33,640
Sent to review: two, one, four runs.

9
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,440
Four happy-path misses in three runs.

10
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:43,980
The control added: a completion guard, pull request nine, that nudges the
model to call send refund.

11
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:46,550
Happy-path misses fell to zero.

12
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:52,750
The regression: the human-reject case went from three of three to zero of
three.

13
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:56,990
The guard kept asking for a refund the human gate had rejected.

14
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,350
The fix, pull request ten, brought it back to three of three.

15
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:04,730
Needs review is zero in all three runs.

16
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:11,070
Open: the already-refunded case fell to zero of three, a label mismatch.

17
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:14,410
The malformed-id case passed one of three.

18
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:18,540
Overall, seventy-five versus seventy-six of eighty-one.

19
00:01:18,710 --> 00:01:21,880
Cost per run: three to eight cents.

20
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:25,950
Median latency: point seven to point nine seconds.

21
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:31,290
Not a clean improvement. Three runs, one model, one prompt.

22
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:33,020
A pilot would tell more.

